desc:GFX G Salem [synth]
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Salem — a pure-synthesis morphing synth (reference, comments only: a pre-Apple Alchemy-style
// synth; no samples, no granular, no spectral file work). Blueprint: the "GFX Lab Morph Synth"
// doc. Built in eight checkpoints; this file is CHECKPOINT 8, all eight built (the playable core, unison, ADD and WT engines, Source B, the pad, the FX,
// the output stage, the CPU pass):
//   - MIDI read in @block into a timed queue, fired at its exact sample
//   - 8 voices as memory records; stealing fades the old note over 3 ms first
//   - VA source: falling polyBLEP saw -> square -> narrow pulse (SHAPE), PWM from a shared LFO
//   - per-voice zero-delay SVF, low -> band -> high (MODE), filter envelope, key tracking
//   - amp + filter ADSR at control rate (every 16 samples), ramped per sample
//   - glide, pitch bend, sustain pedal, all-notes-off
//   - DRIFT (tuning part): each voice's pitch wanders on its own, plus a small random offset
//     per note. (The delay-time part arrives with the FX at checkpoint 6.)
//   - UNISON 1 - 7 copies per voice: DETUNE spread (curved: the outer copies detune most),
//     WIDTH pans them equal-power across the stereo field, PHASE free (random) or reset;
//     a filter per side so the spread survives the filter
//   - ADD engine (checkpoint 3): harmonic sounds - 128 partials baked (inverse FFT) into band-limited
//     tables shared by every voice, 8 levels so each note reads the richest one with nothing above
//     Nyquist; a TILT / EVEN change re-bakes into a spare bank and crossfades in 20 ms. STRETCHED
//     (inharmonic) notes use up to 20 rotating phasors per voice instead - phase-continuous through
//     glide, bend and drift. TILT shapes the spectrum (1 = saw-like, 2 = soft, 0.5 = bright), EVEN sets the even
//     partials (0 = square-like), STRETCH makes it inharmonic (bells, piano-string stretch).
//     Partials fade out as they near Nyquist, so nothing aliases or pops. The engine is chosen
//     per note (VA / ADD / WT keys), so a held note never changes engine mid-sound.
//   - WT engine (checkpoint 4): 8 generated wavetable banks (no samples) of 8 frames each - Classic,
//     Formant (vowels), Organ (drawbars), Digital (stepped), Fold (wavefolder), Sync, PWM, Sweep
//     (moving resonance). Each frame is baked (FFT) into 8 band-limited levels; FRAME morphs between
//     neighbouring frames at the same phase (no cancellation), SWEEP lets the filter envelope move
//     the frame and WOBBLE the mod LFO (its speed is the RATE knob in VA). A bank change bakes in
//     the background (one frame per block) into a spare buffer, then crossfades.
//   - SOURCE B (checkpoint 5): a second source with its own engine (VA / ADD / WT), tables, TUNE and FINE;
//     it shares A's unison, PWM and LFO. The A / B MIX fades equal-power while the two are unrelated
//     and linear as they become alike (a running correlation per voice), so the level holds; a source
//     at zero gain isn't run at all, and B off costs nothing.
//   - TRANSFORM PAD (checkpoint 5): 8 snapshot cells of 16 continuous controls (both sources' shape /
//     tilt / even / frame, the mix, cutoff (blended in octaves), reso, filter env and mode, detune,
//     PWM, width). The puck blends them by inverse distance (SNAP: how sharply each cell pulls),
//     gliding at SLEW. Engines, banks and other switches stay on their keys (no mid-note jumps).
//     Snapshots are saved with the project. The pad is IN from the start: every preset (and a fresh
//     instance) spreads its cells - cell 1 = the preset, the top row opens the filter, the bottom row changes
//     character. Turning a morphed control while the pad plays moves every cell by the same amount;
//     moving the A / B MIX brings Source B in.
//     MOTION: an XY LFO moves the puck on its own, around where you put it - CIRCLE, FIGURE 8,
//     LISSAJOUS (3:2, never quite repeats) or DRIFT (smooth random). MOVE = how far (0 = still),
//     SPEED in Hz. It bounces off the pad's edges, and holds still while a cell is being edited.
//   - FX (checkpoint 6), after the voices, built from the GFX units:
//       DRIVE - the house clipper kit (gfx-clip): drive-tracking pre-filter, anti-aliased soft clipper,
//               BIAS = asymmetry (even harmonics, DC-blocked), TONE = a post low-pass, MIX
//       DELAY - the broadcast-delay engine (gfx-bdelay): Hermite reads, a gliding head; SYNC to the
//               host tempo (1/1 .. 1/32, dotted, triplet) or free; FDBK, DAMP (low-pass in the loop,
//               plus a gentle low cut), SEND (into the line: 0 = let the repeats ring on), MIX;
//               PING = ping-pong (else dual stereo). DRIFT (the master dial) wanders the time a
//               little on each side, like a tape transport (the settled second job of drift).
//       SPACE - the broadcast-reverb engine (gfx-bverb): pre-delay, input diffusion, an 8-line
//               feedback network with three-band decay; SIZE, DECAY, DAMP, MIX, FREEZE (holds the tail).
//     Each IN fades in / out over 10 ms; a unit that's off costs nothing.
// Output: DC blockers (5 Hz) at the start of the master chain and again after the FX, then the house output
// stage (gfx-output), CLIP always on, ceiling -0.3 dBFS. OUT meter: peak hold with its
// figure, and a CLIP lamp that lights while the clipper is working.
// Faceplate: bluish white, silver, blue and cyan, blue LCDs. Presets: 18 + Reset all to defaults.
//
// CPU (checkpoint 8): unison detune / pans worked out once for every voice (only when they change); the pad's blend
// only while the puck moves or something changes; a pure saw skips the pulse; one copy (centred) runs one filter.
// Measured at 8 voices (48 kHz): Init ~5 %, 7-voice unison VA ~10 %, both sources WT + ADD x7 ~25 %, everything
// on (both sources x7 + DRIVE + DELAY + SPACE) ~35 %.
//
// STATUS: Stable v2.0 (from the Lab, Oct 2026). v0.8.2 (checkpoint 8 - complete; reverb wander fix; more space between dials and labels).

import gfx-uimin.jsfx-inc
import gfx-bverb.jsfx-inc
import gfx-bdelay.jsfx-inc
import gfx-clip.jsfx-inc
import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc

out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

slider1:shape=0<0,1,0.001>-Shape (saw > square > pulse)
slider2:pwm=0.15<0,0.45,0.001>-PWM depth
slider3:pwm_hz=0.6<0.05,10,0.01>-PWM rate (Hz)
slider4:cutoff=2400<20,20000,1:log>-Cutoff (Hz)
slider5:reso=0.25<0,1,0.001>-Resonance
slider6:fenv=3<-4,6,0.01>-Filter env (octaves)
slider7:ktrk=0.5<0,1,0.01>-Key tracking
slider8:fmode=0<0,1,0.001>-Filter mode (low > band > high)
slider9:fa=5<0.5,5000,0.1:log>-Filter attack (ms)
slider10:fd=400<1,10000,1:log>-Filter decay (ms)
slider11:fs=30<0,100,0.1>-Filter sustain (%)
slider12:fr=400<1,10000,1:log>-Filter release (ms)
slider13:aa=3<0.5,5000,0.1:log>-Amp attack (ms)
slider14:ad=600<1,10000,1:log>-Amp decay (ms)
slider15:as=80<0,100,0.1>-Amp sustain (%)
slider16:ar=350<1,10000,1:log>-Amp release (ms)
slider17:vsens=0.6<0,1,0.01>-Velocity
slider18:glide=0<0,1000,1>-Glide (ms)
slider19:bend_st=2<0,12,1>-Bend range (semitones)
slider20:drift=50<0,100,1>-Drift (%)
slider21:vol=-6<-24,6,0.1>-Volume (dB)
slider22:uni=1<1,7,1>-Unison (voices)
slider23:detune=12<0,50,0.1>-Unison detune (cents)
slider24:width=70<0,100,1>-Unison width (%)
slider25:phmode=0<0,1,1{Free,Reset}>-Phase
slider26:eng_a=0<0,2,1{VA,ADD,WT}>-Source A engine
slider27:tilt=1<0.3,2.5,0.01>-ADD tilt (1 = saw-like)
slider28:even=1<0,1,0.01>-ADD even partials
slider29:stretch=0<0,1,0.01>-ADD stretch (inharmonic)
slider30:wt_bank=0<0,7,1{Classic,Formant,Organ,Digital,Fold,Sync,PWM,Sweep}>-WT bank
slider31:wt_frame=0<0,7,0.01>-WT frame
slider32:wt_sweep=0<-1,1,0.01>-WT sweep (filter envelope > frame)
slider33:wt_wob=0<0,1,0.01>-WT wobble (mod LFO > frame)
slider34:eng_b=2<0,2,1{VA,ADD,WT}>-Source B engine
slider35:b_shape=0<0,1,0.001>-B shape
slider36:b_tilt=1<0.3,2.5,0.01>-B ADD tilt
slider37:b_even=1<0,1,0.01>-B ADD even partials
slider38:b_stretch=0<0,1,0.01>-B ADD stretch
slider39:b_bank=1<0,7,1{Classic,Formant,Organ,Digital,Fold,Sync,PWM,Sweep}>-B WT bank
slider40:b_frame=0<0,7,0.01>-B WT frame
slider41:b_sweep=0<-1,1,0.01>-B WT sweep
slider42:b_wob=0<0,1,0.01>-B WT wobble
slider43:b_tune=0<-24,24,1>-B tune (semitones)
slider44:b_fine=0<-50,50,0.1>-B fine (cents)
slider45:b_on=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Source B
slider46:ab_mix=0.5<0,1,0.001>-A / B mix
slider47:pad_on=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Transform pad
slider48:pad_x=0.125<0,1,0.001>-Pad X
slider49:pad_y=0.25<0,1,0.001>-Pad Y
slider50:snap=0.3<0,1,0.01>-Pad snap
slider51:slew=200<0,2000,1>-Pad slew (ms)
slider52:drv_on=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Drive
slider53:drv=0.35<0,1,0.001>-Drive amount
slider54:drv_bias=0.4<0,1,0.001>-Drive bias (asymmetry)
slider55:drv_tone=0.55<0,1,0.001>-Drive tone
slider56:drv_mix=1<0,1,0.001>-Drive mix
slider57:dl_on=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay
slider58:dl_sync=1<0,1,1{Free,Sync}>-Delay sync
slider59:dl_ms=375<10,2000,1:log>-Delay time (ms)
slider60:dl_div=8<0,13,1{1/1,1/2,1/2D,1/2T,1/4,1/4D,1/4T,1/8,1/8D,1/8T,1/16,1/16D,1/16T,1/32}>-Delay time (sync)
slider61:dl_fb=0.45<0,0.95,0.001>-Delay feedback
slider62:dl_damp=0.6<0,1,0.001>-Delay damping
